course: dictionary
lesson: 11162
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. The word windmill is a good example: it can name an old building, a modern tower, or a toy.
explain: «Windmills and watermills once ground grain between big stones; today most flour is made in huge roller mills.» Here windmill means a building with sails that the wind turns to grind grain. The clues are grain, stones and flour.
explain: «A wind turbine is a giant windmill.» This time the sentence tells you that a modern windmill is a tall tower that makes electricity. Wind turbine is the more exact name, so when you read windmill in a science book, check the clues.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: A windmill is a building with large sails that the wind turns to grind grain or pump water.
fact: A modern windmill is a tall tower with blades that makes electricity; its more exact name is a wind turbine.
fact: A windmill can also be a toy on a stick with paper or plastic blades that spin in the wind. In the UK this may be called a pinwheel.
fact: Windmill can be a verb too, meaning to swing your arms round and round, but this is rare.
fact: In a famous old story, Don Quixote charges at windmills, thinking they are giants.
exercise: «Windmills and watermills once ground grain between big stones.» In this sentence, what does windmill mean? | A tall tower that makes electricity | *A building with sails that the wind turns to grind grain | A way of swinging your arms round | A toy on a stick with paper blades
exercise: «A wind turbine is a giant windmill.» What does this sentence tell you? | A windmill is a word that only means to swing your arms | A windmill is always a child's toy | A windmill is always used to grind grain | *A windmill can be a modern tower that makes electricity
exercise: Ella runs outside and her paper windmill spins fast in the wind. What is the windmill here? | A tool for pumping water | *A toy on a stick with blades that spin | A tall tower with huge sails | A building where grain is ground
test: What does windmill mean in «A wind turbine is a giant windmill»? | A toy on a stick | A stone building where grain is ground | A way of swinging your arms | *A tall modern tower with blades that makes electricity
test: Which meaning is used when someone says they windmill their arms? | *To swing the arms round and round | To spin in a toy on a stick | To pump water from the ground | To grind grain between stones
exam: Jade reads, «The old windmill turned slowly, grinding corn into flour.» What is the best meaning of windmill here? | To swing your arms round | A toy on a stick | *A building with sails that the wind turns to grind grain | A tall electric tower
